  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Triangle \\(BAD\\) is right-angled at \\(B.\\) On \\(AD\\) there is a point \\(C\\) for which \\(AC=CD\\) and \\(AB=BC.\\) The magnitude of angle \\(DAB,\\) in degrees, is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(67\\dfrac12\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(60\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(45\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(30\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(22\\dfrac12\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": "60"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1963-p6.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\(C\\) is the midpoint of hypotenuse \\(AD,\\) \\(AC=BC=CD.\\) Given \\(AB=BC,\\) triangle \\(ABC\\) is equilateral. Thus \\(\\angle DAB=\\angle CAB=60^\\circ.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "A midpoint of a right triangle’s hypotenuse is equidistant from all three vertices",
        "Use \\(AB=BC=AC\\)"
      ],
